config CANAAN_SND_DESIGNWARE_I2S
	tristate "Canaan K230 Synopsys I2S Device Driver"
	depends on HAVE_CLK
	select SND_SOC_GENERIC_DMAENGINE_PCM
	help
	  This option enables the Canaan fork of the Synopsys I2S device
	  driver (compatible "canaan,snps,designware-i2s"), used by the
	  Canaan K230 SoC's on-die I2S controller. Distinct from mainline's
	  own SND_DESIGNWARE_I2S ("snps,designware-i2s") -- see
	  sound/soc/dwc_canaan/canaan-dwc-i2s.c's own header comment for why
	  this K230 board needs the Canaan variant's register programming,
	  not the generic one.
	  Say Y or M if you have a Canaan K230 Synopsys I2S device in your
	  system.

config CANAAN_SND_DESIGNWARE_PCM
	bool "PCM PIO extension for the Canaan I2S driver"
	depends on CANAAN_SND_DESIGNWARE_I2S
	help
	 Say Y or N if you want to add a custom ALSA extension that registers
	 a PCM and uses PIO to transfer data.
	 This functionality is specially suited for I2S devices that don't have
	 DMA support.
